        "original_id": "ec5510f2-4a51-56a3-a1f3-7793193d510f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Cases: Kessler v. Treat\n- Courts: Supreme Court of the United States\n- People: John Marshall Harlan, Morgan Treat\n- Roles: United States Marshal for the Eastern District of Virginia, Associate Justice\n- Places: Kentucky, Eastern District of Virginia\n\nFacts:\n- John Marshall Harlan was born on June 1, 1833, and he was an American lawyer and politician from Kentucky.\n- John Marshall Harlan served as an associate justice on the U.S. Supreme Court.\n- Kessler v. Treat, 205 U.S. 33 (1907), was a decision of the Supreme Court of the United States.\n- Kessler v. Treat involved allegations that prisoners were unlawfully imprisoned by Morgan Treat, the United States Marshal for the Eastern District of Virginia.\n- In Kessler v. Treat, Justice John Marshall Harlan dissented without writing a separate opinion.",
